%% Message Flow Sequence Diagram
%% Shows step-by-step flow of a payment message through the system

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant App as Banking App
    participant MQ as IBM MQ<br/>GATEWAY.QUEUE
    participant Connector as MQ Source<br/>Connector
    participant SMT as SMT Chain
    participant Kafka as Kafka Topic<br/>PAYMENT_DOMESTIC
    participant Consumer as Payment<br/>Processor

    Note over App,MQ: 1. Message Publishing
    App->>App: Create payment message
    App->>App: Set MQ properties:<br/>messageType=PAYMENT_DOMESTIC<br/>priority=NORMAL<br/>sourceQueue=PAYMENT.DOMESTIC.QUEUE
    App->>MQ: Publish to GATEWAY.QUEUE
    Note right of MQ: Message stored<br/>with properties

    Note over Connector,SMT: 2. Connector Processing
    Connector->>MQ: Poll for messages (every 30s)
    MQ-->>Connector: Return message + properties
    Connector->>Connector: Convert MQ properties<br/>to Kafka headers

    Note over SMT: 3. SMT Transformation
    Connector->>SMT: Pass record
    SMT->>SMT: Transform 1: InsertField<br/>Add kafkaIngestTime
    SMT->>SMT: Transform 2: RegexRouter<br/>Read header: messageType
    SMT->>SMT: Determine target topic:<br/>${header:messageType}<br/>= PAYMENT_DOMESTIC

    Note over SMT,Kafka: 4. Produce to Kafka
    SMT->>Kafka: Produce to PAYMENT_DOMESTIC topic
    Note right of Kafka: Message stored with:<br/>- Headers (from MQ props)<br/>- Key (JMSCorrelationID)<br/>- Value (enriched payload)

    Note over Kafka,Consumer: 5. Consumption
    Consumer->>Kafka: Poll for messages
    Kafka-->>Consumer: Return record
    Consumer->>Consumer: Process payment
    Consumer->>Consumer: Commit offset

    Note over App,Consumer: End-to-End Flow Complete
